// Fixture for the `oskel build` native-fn error test (tests/build_error.cmake).
//
// `getpid` is declared as a `native fn`: the development VM resolves the name
// through its host registry, so this program runs on the VM. The AOT backend has
// no host, and `getpid` has no curated stub, so `oskel build` must fail with the
// dedicated message instead of the generic unassigned-global one a typo
// produces.
//
// It must stay a name the AOT backend has *no* binding for. `clock` used to be
// this fixture's symbol and stopped working as one the moment `clock()` became
// an AOT builtin (BACKLOG §6 item 25), so pick a libc call the runtime does not
// implement -- not a builtin, not one of the curated `sqrt`/`floor`/`ceil`/
// `round` stubs.
native fn getpid(): int;
print(getpid());
